      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CLOSING MODEL (6) has shown good improvement at her last two starts, rewarded with a win last time at this track over 400m. Has good speed so she should be prominent despite the draw. Makes plenty of appeal on the back of that last-start win. SUNSHINE RHONDA (7) was prominent throughout when winning two back but could manage only midfield last time when 4th and beaten 10 lengths at this track (23.46). Form from her last run is proving to be solid. Should play a prominent role. MY OCTAVIUS (1) had been racing well without winning, recording three minors on end before copping a check in the run and finishing seventh in a Grade 5 at this track (23.70). Good beginner and aided by the inside draw. Can measure up this time. ALFIE'S POP (2) can play a role in the finish without surprising.",
